{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Betzal'el made, etc., all the work of, etc.</b> It is difficult: was not even the taking of the donation not yet taken for making, so how can the verse say <b>and he made</b>, etc.? Indeed, the intention is that he prepared the craft tools needed to make with them all the particulars of the work that HaShem commanded to make, for many types of craft tools are required. And this is the verse's measure: <b>And Betzal'el made</b>, etc. <b>all the work of</b> — meaning, tools that constitute the craftwork of <b>the service of the holy place, according to all that HaShem commanded</b> — for there is the work of metals and the work of wooden implements and the work of stones and weaving. And go out and learn from what they said, of blessed memory (Shabbat 49b), that all thirty-nine labors were represented in the Sanctuary, and from what is heard from the verses it is understood that they prepared all the craft tools in a single day."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:02.344509190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}